      "player": "MstLg Stats",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Current hand (7 cards):\n- **Assassin's Strike** {4}{B}{B}: Expensive removal + discard. Not great in an aggressive or tempo deck.\n- **Goblin Wizardry** {3}{R}: Creates two 1/1 Goblin Wizards with prowess. Decent value, but 3 mana is a bit slow.\n- **Kinetic Augur** {3}{R}: 0/4 with trample, power scales with instants/sorceries in graveyard. Discard up to two cards to draw. Strong card advantage engine.\n- **Mountain** (x3): Solid mana base.\n- **Thermo-Alchemist** {1}{R}: 0/3 defender that pings opponents and untaps when you cast instants/sorceries. Good for chip damage and blocking.\n\n**Mulligan Analysis (6-card keep):**\n- **Mana Base:** 3 Mountains is a **strong start**. You’re highly likely to hit your land drops early.\n- **Playable Turn 1:** Thermo-Alchemist (if you want a blocker/pinger) or a Mountain.\n- **Playable Turn 2:** Goblin Wizardry (if you want tokens) or Kinetic Augur (if you want to discard/draw).\n- **Playable Turn 3+:** Assassin's Strike is still expensive, but the rest of the hand is solid.\n- **Redundancy:** Multiple playable cards at each turn, and Thermo-Alchemist provides early interaction.\n\n**Cards to Bottom:**\n- **Assassin's Strike** is the worst card in the hand. It’s too expensive and doesn’t fit the curve or strategy well. The rest of the hand is either mana, early plays, or value engines.\n\n**Verdict:** Bottom **Assassin's Strike**.",
