  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Mulliganed a keepable 7-card hand with 2 lands, two 2-drops (Tinybones, Wight), card filtering (Thrill of Possibility), removal (Hungry Flames), and perfect color fixing. While 2 lands is on the low side, the curve is very low and Thrill helps find more lands. Going to 6 is a meaningful cost.",
      "actionTaken": "Chose to mulligan to 6 cards",
      "betterLine": "Keep the 7-card hand. With two 2-mana plays, Thrill of Possibility to dig for lands, and a low curve, this hand is functional even if you only draw one more land in the first few turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 2,
      "player": "MstLg Stats",
      "decisionIndex": 2
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Casting Alchemist's Gift on Thieves' Guild Enforcer during the precombat main phase when the Enforcer is summoning sick (just entered this turn) accomplishes very little. The +1/+1 buff is temporary (until end of turn), and since the Enforcer can't attack or block this turn, the spell is essentially wasted. The opponent has no attackers threatening damage this turn either. This burns a useful combat trick for no meaningful benefit.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Alchemist's Gift on summoning-sick Thieves' Guild Enforcer with no combat or defensive purpose.",
      "betterLine": "Hold Alchemist's Gift for a future turn when it can be used as a combat trick during actual combat — either to win a favorable trade on attack/block or to grant deathtouch to kill a larger creature. The single black mana could have been left open or the card simply held in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 26,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 12
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chose lifelink on Thieves' Guild Enforcer instead of deathtouch. The Enforcer doesn't currently have deathtouch (opponent only has 2 cards in graveyard, not 8), so choosing deathtouch would have made it a much more threatening blocker/attacker that can trade with any creature. Lifelink on a 2/2 provides marginal life gain at best.",
      "actionTaken": "Chose lifelink for Alchemist's Gift on Thieves' Guild Enforcer",
      "betterLine": "Choose deathtouch - it makes the Enforcer a genuine threat that can trade with any creature, providing far more value than 2 life from lifelink",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 30,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 14
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Gonti, Lord of Luxury before playing the Swamp from hand. By playing the land first, they would have had 5 mana available, leaving 1 mana open after casting Gonti. That floating mana could be relevant for any instant-speed card Gonti exiles from the opponent's library, or for future responses.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Gonti, Lord of Luxury with only 4 lands untapped, using all available mana.",
      "betterLine": "Play Swamp first, then cast Gonti, Lord of Luxury, leaving 1 black mana open for potential instant-speed plays (including whatever card Gonti might exile from the opponent's library).",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 117,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 34
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Player timed out and failed to cast Lightning Visionary from exile (via Gonti's ability, which allows mana of any type to pay for it). With 3 untapped Swamps, they could cast it for {B}{B}. Adding a 2/1 prowess creature to the board is significant when racing at 14 vs 12 life, especially with an empty hand where every resource matters.",
      "actionTaken": "Timed out and passed priority without acting.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Lightning Visionary from exile using two Swamps (Gonti allows any mana type), adding a 2/1 prowess creature to the board for additional pressure.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 177,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 63
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Timed out and failed to cast Lightning Visionary from exile (via Gonti's ability, which allows mana of any type). With 0 cards in hand and 3 untapped Swamps, casting a free 2/1 prowess creature represents significant missed value and board pressure against an opponent at 10 life.",
      "actionTaken": "Timed out and passed priority, ending the turn without taking any action.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Lightning Visionary from exile using 2 Swamps (Gonti allows mana of any type), adding a 2/1 prowess creature to the board for additional pressure.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 188,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 69
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to cast the Gonti-exiled Lightning Visionary (2/1) for 2 mana with 5 untapped Swamps available (Gonti allows any mana type). With the opponent at 6 life, adding a 2/1 body to the board is meaningful additional clock pressure, and there was nothing else to spend the mana on this turn. Finishing Blow costs 5 so it couldn't be cast this turn regardless.",
      "actionTaken": "Timed out and passed the turn without casting Lightning Visionary",
      "betterLine": "Cast Lightning Visionary from exile for {1}{B} using Gonti's mana ability, adding a 2/1 to the board to increase pressure against the opponent at 6 life",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 232,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 89
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 4 life with Stab Wound draining 2 life per upkeep (only 2 turns to live), casting Double Vision for 5 mana does nothing to the board. Wight of Precinct Six would be a 5/5 for just 2 mana (4 creature cards in opponent's graveyard), providing a massive clock to race. Double Vision requires future instants/sorceries to generate value and the player doesn't have time.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Double Vision for 5 mana, spending all available mana on an enchantment that doesn't affect the board",
      "betterLine": "Cast Wight of Precinct Six (5/5 for 2 mana) and Living Lightning (3/2 for 4 mana) - wait, that's 6 mana. Cast Wight of Precinct Six for 2 mana, leaving 3 mana open for future plays, presenting a lethal clock against the opponent at 11 life while racing Stab Wound drain.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 239,
      "player": "MstLg Stats",
      "decisionIndex": 94
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Timed out with opponent at 4 life and all their creatures/lands tapped. Nocturnal Feeder (2/1 flyer) could attack unblocked for 2 damage, putting opponent to 2 life. Dutiful Attendant could also be cast for additional board presence. Missing this turn when so close to lethal is devastating.",
      "actionTaken": "Timed out and did nothing (no response), wasting the entire precombat main phase.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Dutiful Attendant (3 mana), then move to combat and attack with Nocturnal Feeder for 2 unblocked flying damage, putting opponent to 2 life. The opponent would be in a near-unrecoverable position.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 261,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 98
    },
